m's indian  cuisine in a home where meat was never  served her best seller indianish  highlights her culture's colorful dishes  chang's parents immigrated from korea in  the 1960's wow their taste could not be  more different but together they created  a book full of flavor how do you know  this is done and your chicken isn't  overcooked  i just know  we had so many like hours long  conversations of me just being like just  tell me how long to cook the brisket for  and dave being like i can't tell you it  just depends it was  a difficult moment in the creation of  the book  the book is also full of tips like use  your freezer as a pantry you'd be  surprised at what you can chuck in your  freezer you can grate cheddar cheese  throw it in your freezer there's very  little i won't put my freezer now i  basically become my mom because my  freezer is a nightmare things that i was  embarrassed about growing up was like oh  my god i don't want anyone to see what's  in a freezer because  it's like a  taxidermy experience like i don't know  why what  i open the fridge and i'm like oh man i  got like 20 minutes i got to make  something i'm like what do i do when  chang is short on time he speeds things  up in a microwave with a passion that  might surprise you it is a machine from  the future here in present day and  people are like no i don't want to use  it i'm like  want their packages delivered faster  they want to see things on demand but  they want to cook something as slow as  possible  and i have a hard time grasping that  you can't get things crunchy and golden  brown but you can start in the microwave  and then finish it in a pan  on this day they're whipping up chicken  coconut curry  and caccio a pepe  if you do it in a blender it's foolproof  it really is born out of total laziness  so good so good  but a peek at chang's instagram reveals  delicious and nutritious food isn't just  the key to his heart it's who he's  making it for his wife grace and son  hugo hi peppa  i'm eating tacos you're gonna eat  chocolate you love your family you love  cooking i think as a man though too to  show your devotion to your family is a  big thing i never thought i'd be able to  experience the ability to love something  more than myself  it's caused me to realize just how  selfish i was and how i would live my  life and  cooking at home made me understand why i  should be cooking to begin with i love  it now i can't imagine any other way  what do you think hugo good  i'm still learning how to communicate to  my family  the easiest way for me to do it is  through food it's a delicious way yes it  is  dinner's ready thanks hugo for cbs  mornings i'm jamie yucas in los angeles  hungry do you cook you don't cook you  already asked me this during the break i  eat to serve yeah but i'm asking for  them  i don't know if you know that they're  five yeah  i do what i have to do  clearly you cook i love to cook yeah i i  find that taking over the kitchen is is  one of the best uses of my time and you  just said when you're in the kitchen  you're in charge yeah in fact that's one  of the issues sometimes my wife wants to  be in charge of the cooking and i we get  kind of elbow each other out of the way  i'm like out out yeah that's exactly how  it goes one cook at a time yeah i make  too much of a mess yeah we love each  other though all right we'll be right  back  [Music]
 

